# __GURTHANG_PROJECT_NAME__

Generated by Gurthang on Linux. The app is MVC plus an Andurel-style
`src/routes/` layer. Database queries live in the `models` crate.

## Setup

```bash
cp .env.example .env
npm install
gurthang db create
gurthang db migrate up
gurthang run
```

Open <http://127.0.0.1:3000>. `.env` includes `SQLX_OFFLINE=true`. Migrate and
generate/sync refresh `.sqlx` with `cargo sqlx prepare`.

Release builds use Mold via `.cargo/config.toml`. Production:

```bash
gurthang build
APP_ENV=production VITE_DEV_SERVER_URL= target/release/__GURTHANG_PROJECT_NAME__
```

## Layout

- `models/` — `query!` / `query_as!`, factories
- `src/controllers/` — handlers
- `src/routes/` — path, method, name, wiring
- `src/views/` — Inertia page contracts
- `src/services/` — auth and workflows
- `src/jobs/` — typed job enum (SQL stays in `models`)

## Growing the app

```bash
gurthang generate migration create_widgets
gurthang db migrate up
gurthang generate model Widget
gurthang generate scaffold Widget
gurthang generate job SendWelcome
gurthang sync routes
gurthang sync payloads
```

`SQLX_OFFLINE=true cargo check` is the day-to-day compile. Edit a controller
without touching `models/` and the models crate stays cached.

## Jobs

```bash
cargo run
cargo run -- web
cargo run -- worker
```

```rust
use crate::jobs::Job;

let job_id = state.jobs.enqueue(Job::PurgeExpiredSessions).await?;
```
